{
  "_notes": [
    "Guns: rpm and ammo are per gun, set to about 60% of the historical figures for gameplay (slower, chunkier fire). The game merges a battery of guns into a few projectiles per second; damage is per round.",
    "velocity in units/s (1 unit ~ 0.4 m), set from the real muzzle velocity (realVelocity, m/s) as 300 x (real / 770)^1.5, rounded to 5: scaled down for gameplay and the differences stretched, so flat fast guns (M2, Hispano) reach far and slow heavy ones (Type 99, MK 108) need a close target. drop = fraction of gravity felt by the round (slow guns drop more on top), life = seconds before the round is spent (velocity x life is the reach). ammo is the default rounds per gun; a plane's mount can set its own (armament.guns[].ammo).",
    "voice picks the gun sound: rifle | heavy | cannon20 | cannon30."
  ],
